    LLM: 'Game: Aluette. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Aluette (la Vache) is a four-player trick-taking game from VendÃ©e and the coasts of Brittany. Partners sit opposite but do not combine tricks: the team of the individual who wins most tricks (or first to reach that count in a tie) wins the point. Uses a 48-card Spanish-suited pack with a fixed, suit-irrelevant ranking (3s of swords/batons highest down to monsieur/madame lowest). Partners may signal holdings by gestures. Similar to Truc/Put.',
    objective: 'Your team wins the point if one of you takes more tricks than any other single player; if tied, the first to have reached that trick count wins the point for the team.',
    gameplay: 'Left of dealer leads; no suit obligation. Highest card wins trick (ties = trick spoiled, same player leads again). Nine tricks. First to 3 tricks turns a card face up; first to 3 turns two up (to remember order for ties). Partners may signal by agreed gestures.',
